From: V-PACE <yocto@vpace>
Subject: [PATCH] mcap_vendor: link libmcap against zstd

libmcap.so calls zstd (ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter and friends, from the mcap
headers' compressed-chunk writer) but its DT_NEEDED lists only libc, libgcc
and libstdc++. Nothing resolves those symbols at dlopen time, so the mcap
storage plugin aborts as soon as pluginlib actually loads it:

    libmcap.so: undefined symbol: ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter
    [FATAL] No storage could be initialized. Abort

It stays hidden until someone asks for it: rosbag2 defaults to sqlite3, and
`ros2 bag list storage` reads the plugin's XML manifest without dlopening the
library, so mcap is advertised as available regardless.

Upstream mcap_vendor links zstd via `ament_target_dependencies(mcap zstd)`.
meta-ros's 0001-CMakeLists.txt-fetch-dependencies-with-bitbake-fetch.patch
replaced find_package(zstd) with pkg_check_modules(ZSTD libzstd REQUIRED) --
correct for OE -- but reduced that call to `ament_target_dependencies(mcap)`,
i.e. a no-op, leaving the ZSTD_* results it had just computed unused. This
restores the link using them.

target_link_libraries rather than a linker flag because OE builds with
-Wl,--as-needed, which drops -lzstd whenever it precedes the objects that
reference it; only target_link_libraries guarantees the ordering. PRIVATE
because the DT_NEEDED belongs to libmcap.so alone -- keeping it off the
INTERFACE leaves the ament_export_targets(mcap HAS_LIBRARY_TARGET) export
unchanged for rosbag2_storage_mcap, which finds zstd on its own.

This applies on top of the meta-ros patch named above, so it is not a
candidate for upstream.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe specific]

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -51,7 +51,8 @@ macro(build_mcap_vendor)
     "$<BUILD_INTERFACE:${_mcap_include_dir}>"
     "$<INSTALL_INTERFACE:include/${PROJECT_NAME}>"
   )
-  ament_target_dependencies(mcap)
+  target_include_directories(mcap PRIVATE ${ZSTD_INCLUDE_DIRS})
+  target_link_libraries(mcap PRIVATE ${ZSTD_LDFLAGS})
 
   install(
     FILES ${_mcap_installed_headers}
